  $}

  ${
    ifbothdc.1 $e |- ( A = if ( ph , A , B ) -> ( ps <-> th ) ) $.
    ifbothdc.2 $e |- ( B = if ( ph , A , B ) -> ( ch <-> th ) ) $.

    ${
      ifbothdadc.3 $e |- ( ( et /\ ph ) -> ps ) $.
      ifbothdadc.4 $e |- ( ( et /\ -. ph ) -> ch ) $.
      ifbothdadc.dc $e |- ( et -> DECID ph ) $.
      $( A formula ` th ` containing a decidable conditional operator is true
         when both of its cases are true.  (Contributed by Jim Kingdon,
