$)

  $c |_|d $.

  $( Syntax for the domain-disjoint-union of two relations. $)
  cdjud $a class ( R |_|d S ) $.

  $( The "domain-disjoint-union" of two relations: if ` R C_ ( A X. X ) ` and
     ` S C_ ( B X. X ) ` are two binary relations, then ` ( R |_|d S ) ` is the
     binary relation from ` ( A |_| B ) ` to ` X ` having the universal
     property of disjoint unions (see ~ updjud in the case of functions).

     Remark: the restrictions to ` dom R ` (resp. ` dom S ` ) are not necessary
     since extra stuff would be thrown away in the post-composition with ` R `
     (resp. ` S ` ), as in ~ df-case , but they are explicitly written for
     clarity.  (Contributed by MC and BJ, 10-Jul-2022.) $)
