       in Section 3.1 of [Pierik], p. 15.  If we assumed excluded middle, this
       would be essentially the same as ` NN0* ` as defined at ~ df-xnn0 but in
       its absence the relationship between the two is more complicated.  This
       definition would function much the same whether we used ` _om ` or
       ` NN0 ` , but the former allows us to take advantage of
       ` 2o = { (/) , 1o } ` ( ~ df2o3 ) so we adopt it.  (Contributed by Jim
       Kingdon, 14-Jul-2022.) $)
    df-nninf $a |- NN+oo = { f e. ( 2o ^m _om ) |
      A. i e. _om ( f ` suc i ) C_ ( f ` i ) } $.
  $}

