  ${
    $d f i j x y z $.

    $( Real number trichotomy implies the Limited Principle of Omniscience
       (LPO).  We expect that we'd need some form of countable choice to prove
       the converse.

       Here's the outline of the proof.  Given an infinite sequence F of zeroes
       and ones, we need to show the sequence contains a zero or it is all
       ones.  Construct a real number A whose representation in base two
       consists of a zero, a decimal point, and then the numbers of the
       sequence.  Compare it with one using trichotomy.  The three cases from
       trichotomy are ~ trilpolemlt1 (which means the sequence contains a
       zero), ~ trilpolemeq1 (which means the sequence is all ones), and
       ~ trilpolemgt1 (which is not possible).

       Equivalent ways to state real number trichotomy (sometimes called
       "analytic LPO") include decidability of real number apartness (see
       ~ triap ) or that the real numbers are a discrete field (see
       ~ trirec0 ).

       LPO is known to not be provable in IZF (and most constructive
       foundations), so this theorem establishes that we will be unable to
       prove an analogue to ~ qtri3or for real numbers.  (Contributed by Jim
       Kingdon, 23-Aug-2023.) $)
    trilpo $p |- ( A. x e. RR A. y e. RR ( x < y \/ x = y \/ y < x )
        -> _om e. Omni ) $=
      ( vz vf vi vj cv clt wbr wceq w3o cr wral cn wcel com cfv c1 co c2 cc0 wo
      comni wrex cpr cmap wa cexp cdiv cmul wf elmapi adantl oveq2 oveq2d fveq2
      csu oveq12d cbvsumv trilpolemcl simpl breq1 eqeq1 breq2 3orbi123d rspc2va
      1red eqeq2 syl21anc trilpolemres ralrimiva cvv nnex isomninn ax-mp sylibr
      wb cen nnenom enomni sylib ) AGZBGZHIZWBWCJZWCWBHIZKZBLMALMZNUCOZPUCOZWHC
      GDGZQZUAJCNUDWLRJCNMUBZDUARUEZNUFSZMZWIWHWMDWOWHWKWOOZUGZCNRTEGZUHSZUISZW
